Moser, 30 unit vectors: 60 ordered triples with g1 + g2 = g3   e.g. #0 + #10 = #5
Haugland, 42 unit vectors: 84 ordered triples with g1 + g2 = g3   e.g. #0 + #14 = #7

both lattices carry a unit triangle, so Proposition 23's cyclic half
applies at every a = 4m^2, for either of them.

     a   m   |h_g| = m|1-theta_a|   m even kills Z/4
     4   1         0.500000000000  needs the triangle
    16   2         0.500000000000                yes
    36   3         0.500000000000  needs the triangle
    64   4         0.500000000000                yes
   100   5         0.500000000000  needs the triangle
   144   6         0.500000000000                yes

every h_g has length exactly 1/2, so 2h_g is a unit vector of the joint
lattice and any Z/4 homomorphism must give h_g an odd value.
